t\t\t\t\t>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tFact Sheets\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</li>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<li class=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-item\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tclass=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-link is-current\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\thref=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/releases/\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\taria-label=\"Releases\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tReleases\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</li>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<li class=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-item\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tclass=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-link\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\thref=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/remarks/\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\taria-label=\"Remarks\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tRemarks\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</li>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<li class=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-item\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tclass=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-link\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\thref=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/research/\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\taria-label=\"Research\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tResearch\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</li>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</ul>\n\t\t</div>\n\t</nav>\n\t</div>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>Today, President Donald J. Trump stood with the families of murder victims to condemn Gov. Gavin Newsom’s gutless decision to wipe out the death sentences of all 548 inmates on California’s death row.</strong> Two days after the election, Newsom <a href=\"https://www.gov.ca.gov/2026/11/05/governor-newsom-releases-letter-to-california-on-the-death-penalty/\">handed</a> blanket clemency to child killers, serial murderers, and cop killers, and the victims’ families say they were never even told — a shameful abdication of basic responsibility and integrity that defines today’s Democrat Party.</p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>“Face me, Gov. Newsom. Tell me Michael’s life doesn’t matter. Michael deserved a Governor who would stand with the victims, honor their justice, and respect the will of the people. You may have taken our justice, but you will never take Michael’s voice,”</strong> <a href=\"https://x.com/RapidResponse47/status/2124985042929700879\">said</a> Sandy Friend, whose son, Michael Lyons, was kidnapped, tortured, and brutally murdered at just 8-years-old.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>“For three decades, our family lived with the understanding that the justice system’s decision would stand. Today, I stand before you outraged — outraged — that Gov. Gavin Newsom unilaterally erased that sentence,”</strong> <a href=\"https://x.com/RapidResponse47/status/2124986759905681765\">said</a> Marc Klaas, whose 12-year-old daughter, Polly, was abducted at knifepoint and strangled.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>“Gov. Newsom, under the cloak of darkness, unilaterally makes a decision to commute the sentences of the most heinous criminals in our society. I am disgusted and frustrated. My brother did not die in vain,”</strong> <a href=\"https://x.com/RapidResponse47/status/2124991596479545450\">said</a> Lt. Jason Davis, whose brother was killed in the line of duty by a depraved illegal alien.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>“My dad was more than a police officer. He was a loving father, a grandfather, a public servant, and a friend to many. I am incredibly proud to be his daughter, and his love, sacrifice, and legacy will stay with me forever,</strong>” <a href=\"https://x.com/RapidResponse47/status/2124989416485904806\">said</a> Gloria Vega, whose father, Officer Jose “Gil” Vega, was murdered in the line of duty just months before he was set to retire.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>Meet the Monsters Newsom Is Fighting to Spare:</strong></p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Marcus Wesson</strong> murdered nine of his own children and grandchildren — the youngest just a year old — and raped and molested his daughters and nieces inside the cult-like family he controlled for years.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Richard Allen Davis</strong> snatched 12-year-old Polly Klaas at knifepoint from a slumber party in her own home and strangled her.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Isauro Aguirre</strong> tortured 8-year-old Gabriel Fernandez for months, then beat him to death — leaving him with a fractured skull, a dozen broken ribs, and burns.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>David Westerfield</strong> kidnapped 7-year-old Danielle van Dam from her own San Diego bedroom and murdered her.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Charles Ng</strong> tortured and sexually abused women on videotape at a remote Sierra foothills cabin and slaughtered 11 people — including two baby boys.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Randy Kraft</strong> murdered 16 young men, sexually mutilating them and dumping their bodies along Southern California freeways before police caught him with a dead Marine in his passenger seat.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Chester Turner</strong> raped and strangled 14 women in South Los Angeles over more than a decade, becoming the city’s most prolific serial killer.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Vincent Brothers</strong> slaughtered his wife, Joanie, her mother, and their three children — Marques, 4, Lyndsey, 2, and 6-week-old Marshall — in their Bakersfield home.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Ramon Salcido</strong> slit the throats of his daughters Sofia, 4, and Teresa, 1, then murdered his wife, her mother, her two young sisters, and a co-worker.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Cary Stayner</strong> murdered Carole Sund, her 15-year-old daughter, Juli, and 16-year-old Silvina Pelosso near Yosemite in 1999.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Luis Bracamontes</strong>, a twice-deported killer, gunned down Sacramento County Deputy Danny Oliver and Placer County Detective Michael Davis, Jr., in 2014 — then told the court he wished he had killed more.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Daniel Wozniak</strong> shot his neighbor, 26-year-old Army veteran Sam Herr, to bankroll his own wedding, dismembered his body, then lured Herr’s friend Julie Kibuishi, 23, and murdered her to frame him.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">That Newsom would even consider sparing these killers tells you everything you need to know about the sickness and depravity that runs through the Democrat Party.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/releases/2026/11/president-trump-stands-with-victims-families-as-newsom-grants-mass-clemency-to-depraved-killers/\">President Trump Stands with Victims’ Families as Newsom Grants Mass Clemency to Depraved Killers</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov\">The White House</a>.</p>",
